# Planner consumer #1 — REGRESSION GUARD for the `is_bare_param` gate. The same
# program as `cow_loop_bare_param_if_branch` but with a `&` (mutable-borrow)
# param: `&` writes THROUGH to the caller and must NOT be materialized. The
# dispatch-arm hoist is gated on `is_bare_param` (false for `&`/`!` params), so
# no private copy is made — the pop is visible to the caller. Both f and main
# print 3 (contrast the bare-param fixture's 3,4). ggdef-adjudicated 3,3.
void f(Vector[int] &xs):
    if xs.len() > 2:
        xs.pop()
    print(xs.len())

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3, 4]
    f(&a)
    print(a.len())
